This has been asked for a couple of times. Basically you can construct
the source document dynamically and knit it later (e.g.
https://groups.google.com/group/knitr/browse_thread/thread/e46d09dd314794ea).

Here is an example for Markdown, and you can change pat_md() to
pat_rnw(), render_markdown() to render_listings() respectively for Rnw
documents:

https://github.com/yihui/knitr-examples/blob/master/041-label-i.Rmd
https://github.com/yihui/knitr-examples/blob/master/041-label-i-child.tpl

The brew package is so influential that people often ignore the fact
that knitr also supports the <% %> syntax :)

