>
> Because the mdframed environment disrupts the float, it has to be called
> INSIDE LaTeX's \figure{} environment or LaTeX complains that I'm calling a
> float (the figure) while not in 'outer par' mode.
>
> So I'm using a knitr_hook to add the environment calls either side of the
> \includegraphics command, like this:
>
> knit_hooks$set(roundFrame = function(before, options, envir) {
>    if (before) {
>   name = paste(options$fig.path, options$label, sep = '')
>   return(paste('\\begin{mdframed}[roundcorner=7pt] \n \\includegraphics{',
> name, '} \n \\end{mdframed} \n', sep = ''))
>      } })
>
> That seems to work (although I can't seem to control the output width of the
> r.plot).
>
